 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 510442,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Write the numbers of base 4 up to 100<sub>4</sub>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0, 1, 2, 3<br>\n10, 11, 12, 13<br>\n20, 21, 22, 23<br>\n30, 31, 32, 33<br>\n100"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>There are four digits in the base four system:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0,1,2,3.\"></span></p>\n<p>When you run out of digits, you need two digits. Because the place value is 4 in the base 4 system, start with a 1 in the 4s place.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"10,11,12,13\"></span></p>\n<p>Now, add 2 in the 4s place.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"20,21,22,23\"></span></p>\n<p>Now, write 3 in the 4s place.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"30,31,32,33\"></span></p>\n<p>Now, you have run out of digits in the 4s place. Now, you move over to the <span data-math=\"{4^2}\"></span> place.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"100\"></span></p>\n<p>This is where you were told to stop.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
